<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa retail sales rise 1.2 pct m/m in February.</title>
<headline>S.Africa retail sales rise 1.2 pct m/m in February.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African retail trade sales rose a seasonally adjusted 1.2 percent month-on-month in February to 11.56 billion rand, latest Central Statistical Service (CSS) data shows.</p>
<p>Year-on-year, seasonally adjusted retail sales were up 11.1 percent from 10.4 billion rand in February 1996, the CSS said.</p>
<p>On an actual basis, retail trade sales were down 0.4 percent month-on-month and up 11.0 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Retail trade sales at current prices.</p>
<p>(rand million):</p>
<p>				    Feb '97   Jan '97     Feb '96</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted     11,561.1  11,422.2    10,402.0</p>
<p>    Actual			10,079.1  10,120.3     9,077.1</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003 --</p>
